        "original_id": "74087729-22e2-5965-9ff2-aff35dffd1b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Chvrches, Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie\n- People: Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, Martin Doherty, Martin Metcalfe, John Duncan, Fin Wilson, Shirley Manson, Rona Scobie, Derek Kelly\n- Songs: \"Make Them Gold\"\n- Albums: Every Open Eye\n- Places: Bathgate, Edinburgh, Scotland\n- Topics: band lineups, music genres\n\nFacts:\n- Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie was a Scottish rock group active in the 1980s and 1990s that was formed in Bathgate near Edinburgh, Scotland.\n- At Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie's commercial peak, Martin Metcalfe was on vocals, John Duncan was on guitar, Fin Wilson was on bass guitar, Shirley Manson and Rona Scobie were on keyboards and backing vocals, and Derek Kelly was on drums.\n- Chvrches consists of Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, and Martin Doherty.\n- In Chvrches, Lauren Mayberry performs lead vocals, drums, additional synthesisers, and samplers.\n- In Chvrches, Iain Cook performs synthesisers, guitar, bass, and vocals.\n- In Chvrches, Martin Doherty performs synthesisers, samplers, and vocals.\n- \"Make Them Gold\" is a song by the Scottish synthpop band Chvrches.\n- \"Make Them Gold\" appears on Chvrches' second studio album, Every Open Eye.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
